.TH webhttrack 1 "@DATE@" "httrack website copier"
.SH NAME
webhttrack \- offline browser : copy websites to a local directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
@SYNOPSIS@
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B webhttrack
starts the
.BR htsserver (1)
web server and opens the WebHTTrack interface in a browser. The interface drives the
.BR httrack (1)
engine to copy websites to a local directory, by default
.IR ~/websites .
The server stops once the interface is closed.
.SH OPTIONS
@OPTIONS@
.SH EXAMPLES
@EXAMPLES@
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP BROWSER
The browser to open, through xdg\-open or sensible\-browser. Without it,
.B webhttrack
tries a list of known browsers.
.IP "LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, LANG"
The first one set picks the language of the interface, until the interface saves its own choice in
.IR ~/.httrack.ini .
.IP HOME
Projects are kept in
.I ~/websites
unless the interface has saved another folder.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.httrack.ini
.RS
The interface settings. Its
.I path=
line names the projects directory that
.I browse
opens.
.RE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Each mirror writes its errors and warnings to
.I hts\-log.txt
in the project directory.
@FOOTER@
.PP
The server is
.BR htsserver (1),
and the command-line engine is
.BR httrack (1).
